   103	
   104	/**
   105	 Specifies if the standard user driver should handle showing a new scheduled update, or if its delegate should handle showing the update instead.
   106	 
   107	 If you implement this method and return @c NO the delegate is then responsible for showing the update,
   108	 which must be implemented and done in `-standardUserDriverWillHandleShowingUpdate:forUpdate:state:`
   109	 The motivation for the delegate being responsible for showing updates is to override Sparkle's default behavior
   110	 and add gentle reminders for new updates.
   111	 
   112	 Returning @c YES is the default behavior and allows the standard user driver to handle showing the update.
   113	 
   114	 If the standard user driver handles showing the update, `immediateFocus` reflects whether or not it will show the update in immediate and utmost focus.
   115	 The standard user driver may choose to show the update in immediate and utmost focus when the app was launched recently
   116	 or the system has been idle for some time.
   117	 
   118	 If `immediateFocus` is @c NO the standard user driver may want to defer showing the update until the user comes back to the app.
   119	 For background running applications, when `immediateFocus` is  @c NO the standard user driver will always want to show
   120	 the update alert immediately, but behind other running applications or behind the app's own windows if it's currently active.
   121	 
   122	 There should be no side effects made when implementing this method so you should just return @c YES or @c NO
   123	 You will also want to implement `-standardUserDriverWillHandleShowingUpdate:forUpdate:state:` for adding additional update reminders.
   124	 
   125	 This method is not called for user-initiated update checks. The standard user driver always handles those.
   126	 
   127	 Visit https://sparkle-project.org/documentation/gentle-reminders for more information and examples.
   128	 
   129	 @param update The update the standard user driver should show.
   130	 @param immediateFocus If @c immediateFocus is @c YES, then the standard user driver proposes to show the update in immediate and utmost focus. See discussion for more details.
   131	 
   132	 @return @c YES if the standard user should handle showing the scheduled update (default behavior), otherwise @c NO if the delegate handles showing it.
   133	 */
   134	- (BOOL)standardUserDriverShouldHandleShowingScheduledUpdate:(SUAppcastItem *)update andInImmediateFocus:(BOOL)immediateFocus;
   135	
   136	/**
   137	 Called before an update will be shown to the user.
   138	 
   139	 If the standard user driver handles showing the update, `handleShowingUpdate` will be `YES`.
   140	 Please see `-standardUserDriverShouldHandleShowingScheduledUpdate:andInImmediateFocus:` for how the standard user driver
   141	 may handle showing scheduled updates when `handleShowingUpdate` is `YES` and `state.userInitiated` is `NO`.
   142	 
   143	 If the delegate declared it handles showing the update by returning @c NO in `-standardUserDriverShouldHandleShowingScheduledUpdate:andInImmediateFocus:`
   144	 then the delegate should handle showing update reminders in this method, or at some later point.
   145	 In this case, `handleShowingUpdate` will be @c NO.
   146	 To bring the update alert in focus, you may call `-[SPUStandardUpdaterController checkForUpdates:]` or `-[SPUUpdater checkForUpdates]`.
   147	 You may want to show additional UI indicators in your application that will show this update in focus
   148	 and want to dismiss additional UI indicators in `-standardUserDriverWillFinishUpdateSession` or `-standardUserDriverDidReceiveUserAttentionForUpdate:`
   149	  
   150	 If `state.userInitiated` is @c YES then the standard user driver always handles showing the new update and `handleShowingUpdate` will be @c YES.
   151	 In this case, it may still be useful for the delegate to intercept this method right before a new update will be shown.
   152	 
   153	 This method is not called when bringing an update that has already been presented back in focus.
   154	 
   155	 Visit https://sparkle-project.org/documentation/gentle-reminders for more information and examples.
   156	 
   157	 @param handleShowingUpdate @c YES if the standard user driver handles showing the update, otherwise @c NO if the delegate handles showing the update.
   158	 @param update The update that will be shown.
   159	 @param state The user state of the update which includes if the update check was initiated by the user.
   160	 */
   161	- (void)standardUserDriverWillHandleShowingUpdate:(BOOL)handleShowingUpdate forUpdate:(SUAppcastItem *)update state:(SPUUserUpdateState *)state;
